= Common Errors and Special Cases

#exception-box(title: "Common Errors & Special Cases")[
  #table(
    columns: (1.35fr, 1.35fr, 1.2fr),
    table.header[*The mistake students make*][*What is right*][*The why / the trap*],
    ["Marketing and selling mean the same"], [Selling is *one function inside* marketing; marketing starts before production], [The focus test decides: needs vs product.],
    ["Expensive products are specialty goods"], [The class follows *buying effort*, not price alone], [A costly item bought casually with little comparison is not specialty — effort is the test.],
    ["Channel level counts every member"], [Count only the *middlemen* between producer and consumer], [A zero-level channel has no middleman — producer to consumer directly.],
    ["Advertising always raises prices"], [Mass advertising builds volume that *lowers* per-unit cost — the standard reply], [Cost per contact falls as reach grows; misuse of ads is a separate issue.],
    ["Warehousing and transportation are the same component"], [Warehousing creates *time* utility; transportation creates *place* utility], [Storing waits for demand; moving reaches it.],
    ["The societal concept and marketing concept are the same"], [Societal adds *society's welfare* — environment, ethics — on top of customer satisfaction], [The widest lens of the five philosophies.],
  )
]

- *Spot the pattern:* classification rules this unit — goods classes, channel
  levels, promotion tools, philosophy eras. Learn each class by its *test*
  (effort, middlemen, payment, era) and the shuffles collapse.
- *One special case:* "the producer sells through the company's own website"
  is a *zero-level (direct)* channel — the website is the producer itself,
  not a middleman.

