= Practice Questions

#mcq(1, [Marketing is best described as:], (
  [selling goods at the highest possible price], [a social process of identifying needs and satisfying them profitably — beginning before production and continuing after the sale], [advertising a product on television], [transporting goods to warehouses],
))

#mcq(2, [Which philosophy of marketing holds that buyers will favour products of high quality that are improved over time, without studying what buyers actually want?], (
  [production concept], [product concept], [selling concept], [marketing concept],
))

#mcq(3, [Which statement correctly distinguishes marketing from selling?], (
  [selling starts before production; marketing after it], [marketing focuses on customer needs while selling focuses on the product], [marketing is narrower in scope than selling], [selling aims at satisfaction while marketing aims at volume only],
))

#mcq(4, [Bread, soap and newspapers that are bought frequently with minimum effort are classified as:], (
  [shopping goods], [specialty goods], [convenience goods], [industrial goods],
))

#mcq(5, [The written tag on a product giving its contents, weight, usage and warnings is the:], (
  [brand], [label], [package], [trademark],
))

#mcq(6, [Which factor of pricing sets the *floor* below which the firm cannot price for long?], (
  [utility of the product], [cost of the product], [government regulation], [marketing method],
))

#mcq(7, [A dairy delivers milk directly to consumers through its own vans and website. The channel level is:], (
  [one-level], [two-level], [zero-level — direct channel], [three-level],
))

#mcq(8, [The component of physical distribution that creates *time utility* by holding goods until demand arrives is:], (
  [transportation], [warehousing], [order processing], [inventory financing],
))

#mcq(9, [A company distributes free samples of a new shampoo alongside a festival discount coupon. The promotion tool being used is:], (
  [public relations], [personal selling], [sales promotion], [advertising],
))

#mcq(10, ["Advertising raises the cost of the product" is an objection whose standard reply is:], (
  [advertising never costs anything], [large-scale advertising builds sales volume that lowers per-unit cost], [all advertised products are of poor quality], [only inferior products need advertising],
))

= Solutions

#solution(1, [Marketing is the *social process* of identifying needs and satisfying them profitably — it begins with need study *before* production and continues with service *after* the sale. Advertising and transport are single functions within it.], answer: "B")

#solution(2, [The *product concept* trusts quality and improvement to sell themselves — the trap being that buyers may want something else entirely. The marketing concept studies the buyer first.], answer: "B")

#solution(3, [The focus test: marketing centres on *customer needs*, selling on *the product*; marketing begins before production and includes selling as one part of its wider scope.], answer: "B")

#solution(4, [Frequent purchase with *minimum effort* defines *convenience goods* — wide distribution and low unit prices follow. Shopping goods are compared; specialty goods take special effort.], answer: "C")

#solution(5, [The *label* is the written information carrier — identity, contents, usage, warnings. The brand identifies; the package protects and promotes.], answer: "B")

#solution(6, [*Cost* — fixed plus variable — sets the floor: sustained pricing below total cost bleeds the firm. Utility and demand set the ceiling instead.], answer: "B")

#solution(7, [No middleman stands between producer and consumer when the firm's *own* vans and website deliver — a *zero-level (direct)* channel. Count middlemen, not touchpoints.], answer: "C")

#solution(8, [*Warehousing* holds goods until they are needed — creating *time utility*. Transportation creates place utility; order processing speeds the paperwork.], answer: "B")

#solution(9, [Free samples and festival coupons are *short-run incentives to buy now* — the signature of *sales promotion*. Advertising informs at mass scale; PR builds image without payment.], answer: "C")

#solution(10, [The standard reply: mass advertising *builds volume*, and higher volume *lowers per-unit cost* — so the added advertising cost is spread thinner, not simply passed on.], answer: "B")

